.TH BAIDUPCSR-CLI 1 "2026-05-18" "baidupcsr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
baidupcsr-cli \- Rust terminal UI for BaiduPCS-Go accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B baidupcsr-cli
[\fBtui\fR]
.br
.B baidupcsr-cli doctor
[\fB--redact\fR] [\fB--config-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B baidupcsr-cli
starts a Ratatui-based remote file manager backed by an existing
BaiduPCS-Go configuration. Runtime data comes from the configured account and
remote read/write APIs; the TUI does not fall back to mock directory data.
.PP
The Go configuration file is read-only. Rust-specific UI settings and directory
cache data are stored separately.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Start the interactive TUI. This is also the default command when no argument is
provided.
.TP
.B doctor
Print redacted configuration, cache, video preview, player, and permission
diagnostics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --redact
Keep diagnostic output in the redacted mode. This is the default for
.B doctor
and is kept as an explicit flag for scripts.
.TP
.BI --config-dir " DIR"
Read BaiduPCS-Go configuration from
.IR DIR /pcs_config.json .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BAIDUPCS_GO_CONFIG_DIR
Directory containing BaiduPCS-Go
.IR pcs_config.json .
.TP
.B BAIDUPCSR_UI_CONFIG
Path to the Rust sidecar UI config.
.TP
.B BAIDUPCSR_CACHE_DIR
Directory for baidupcsr persistent directory cache.
.TP
.B BAIDUPCSR_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Directory for explicit download tasks.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/BaiduPCS-Go/pcs_config.json
Default BaiduPCS-Go config path on Unix.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/baidupcsr/ui_config.toml
Default Rust sidecar UI config path.
.TP
.I $HOME/.cache/baidupcsr
Default Rust directory cache path when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is not set.
.SH SECURITY
Credential values such as Cookie, BDUSS, STOKEN, access tokens, dlinks, and
private video tokens must not be printed by diagnostics or validation records.
Preview is read-only by default. Explicit download tasks are the path that
writes remote file content to disk.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR bash (1)
